+# CTRLCAP replay criterion
+
+Status: `DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`.
+
+The diagnostic is complete only when one deterministic command using one parent and at most two independent anchor workers (three Python processes, below the hard cap of four):
+
+1. reconstructs both rules' fixed `J_from_first` assignments on all eight anchors and all 48 realised boundaries;
+2. replays C1 and fails closed if any reported C1 floating value differs by more than 2 ULP or any reported count differs;
+3. replays each recorded C2 local-search mode schedule and requires its aggregate values and counts to match the sealed control-law receipt within the same 2-ULP tolerance;
+4. integrates delivery per user-anchor before computing `CAPACITY`, `DEMAND_CAPPED`, and `ATTAINMENT_ONLY`;
+5. enumerates every integrated-delivery non-regression violation, reconciles the attainment-defined cohort split, and exactly decomposes the capped relative gain into energy-only and extra-credited-bits components; and
+6. writes `.scratch/control-law-capped/rescored.json` and `CONTROL-LAW-DEMAND-CAPPED-2026-09-10.md` without changing any source receipt, sealed setting, search setting, or sibling workspace.

