# CTRLCAP — demand-capped fixed-assignment control-law headroom

`DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM` · recorded assignments · unchanged deterministic C2 search replay

## Verified by running code

### Parity gate and invariant

C1 replay passed the controller-declared 2-ULP gate: 54 of 54 floating fields were exact, 0 differed by 1 ULP, 0 by 2 ULP, and 0 exceeded 2 ULP (maximum 0 ULP). All 36 C1 count fields matched exactly.

As a schedule-identity cross-check, C2 replay had 46 of 54 floating fields exact, 4 at 1 ULP, 4 at 2 ULP, and 0 above 2 ULP (maximum 2 ULP); all 36 C2 counts matched.

The integrated-delivery invariant holds for all 1600 user-anchors across both rules: 2 violations. The minimum observed `C2 − C1` delivery was -0.000000 Mbit.

### Three numerators

Each user's 48 boundary values were trapezoid-integrated over 47 × 0.640 s = 30.08 s first. The 1.504 Gbit cap or attainment filter was then applied per user-anchor, followed by pooling across users and all eight anchors.

